{"name":"Front Porch","hex":"#cdccc5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"front porch","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A porch at the front of a building.","A brief period inserted between the end of each transmitted line of picture and the leading edge of the next line sync pulse, intended to allow voltage levels to stabilise in older televisions, preventing interference between picture lines."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/front_porch"}],"entries":[{"title":"Front Porch","blocks":[{"text":"Front Porch is the sixth studio album by American singer-songwriter Joy Williams. It was released on May 3, 2019 by Sensibility Recordings. It was nominated for Best Folk Album at the 62nd Grammy Awards."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/22/Joy_Williams_-_Front_Porch.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Front_Porch","wikidata":"Q63921072"},{"title":"Porch","blocks":[{"text":"A porch is a room or gallery located in front of an entrance to a building. A porch is placed in front of the façade of a building it commands, and forms a low front. Alternatively, it may be a vestibule or a projecting building that houses the entrance door of a building."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Chartres_Cathedral_020_south_facade_TTaylor.JPG/330px-Chartres_Cathedral_020_south_facade_TTaylor.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Porch","wikidata":"Q816741"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/London_-_Cromwell_Road_-_Natural_History_Museum_1881_by_Alfred_Waterhouse_-_View_NW_%26_Up_at_the_Entrance_on_the_Terracotta_Tiled_Fa%C3%A7ade.jpg/500px-London_-_Cromwell_Road_-_Natural_History_Museum_1881_by_Alfred_Waterhouse_-_View_NW_%26_Up_at_the_Entrance_on_the_Terracotta_Tiled_Fa%C3%A7ade.jpg?utm_sour